  "conclusion": "17 of 18 runs succeeded on RTX 4090 with zero dense fallbacks and zero black frames (all with AAC 32kHz stereo audio, RMS -13.78 to -15.76 dB). Sol-Attn unlocked native 1080p (1920x1088->1080) 5s 2-step generation in 100.23s (22.5 GB Peak VRAM) and 30s (719f) 480p T2V/FL2VA in ~337-347s. 768p 30s hit 24GB VRAM OOM, establishing 480p as the practical 30s ceiling on 24GB. For 4-step generation (10s T2V, 5s/10s FL2VA), Spark-Attn SM89 outperformed Sol-Attn by 25-36% (e.g., 54.65s vs 72.52s on 5s FL2VA; 124.70s vs 196.04s on 10s T2V; 133.22s on 10s FL2VA).",
